<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulf of Mirabello</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mirabello Bay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulf of Mirabello is a large bay on the north coast of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. The ancient cities of Lato and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olous">Olous</a>, the Minoan town of Gournia and the modern town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agios-nikolaos">Agios Nikolaos</a> lie on or near its shores. Its name comes from a Venetian fortress, Mirabello, that stood above the harbour of Agios Nikolaos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mirabello.jpg" alt="Gulf of Mirabello" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ingo Wölbern · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kueste_Kreta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
